# SPA fallback: every unmatched path serves the app shell (200, not a client
# redirect) so React Router can handle client-side routes like
# /m/<a>-v-<b>/<seed> on a cold/hard-refresh load. The /m/* Cloudflare Pages
# Function still runs first and falls through to this same rule via
# context.next().
#
# Target is "/", not "/index.html" — the latter trips Cloudflare's redirect
# loop detector (it can be rewritten back to "/" by the platform's own clean-
# URL handling, which then matches this same "/*" pattern again). Verified
# locally with `wrangler pages dev`: "/index.html" gets the whole rule
# silently discarded ("0 valid redirect rules"); "/" parses and serves
# correctly, including for the /m/* permalink route.
/*    /   200
